# Design system source of truth

The project’s UI source of truth is:

**[`docs/cursor-design-system.html`](docs/cursor-design-system.html)** (Cursor Design System v3)

## Priority

1. **`docs/cursor-design-system.html`** — tokens, type, spacing, components, and visual rules. Follow this first.
2. **Figma personal-finance-app** (see `.cursor/skills/figma-fin-design`) — layout/structure and product screens. Use for screen composition and missing specifics.
3. **Existing app code** — match local patterns only when they already align with (1), or when updating them toward (1).

When Figma (or existing code) conflicts with the Cursor design system doc — colors, type, radius, spacing, accent usage, card treatment, etc. — **prefer the Cursor design system**.

## When implementing UI

- Read the relevant sections of `docs/cursor-design-system.html` before inventing styles.
- Prefer the CSS custom properties defined in that doc (`--bg-base`, `--accent`, `--text-primary`, type scale, spacing, radii).
- Do not reintroduce competing palettes or generic AI-default looks that contradict the doc.
